{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The source explicitly identifies “匕” as the sound cue, but its historical readings are only similar in Baxter–Sagart’s system: 比 *C.pijʔ versus 匕 *pijʔ. The Shang phrase also has competing readings, including 李宗焜’s “assist/support” proposal, so I’m keeping both the book’s construction and meaning account attributed rather than treating either as settled."}}
